00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:45.740
Since January Dylan has been finding it much more difficult to make ends meet

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:51.100
because of a new California law that limits the extent to which companies can use contract labor.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:56.720
California Assembly Bill Five was designed to constrain the growth of the so called gig economy

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:03.280
based on the theory that companies like Uber, Lyft, and Postmates are taking advantage of contract labor.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:08.100
The bill was authored by Assemblywoman Lorena Gonzalez, a former union leader who declined

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:14.120
Reasons interview request. It was passed last September with strong support from organized labor.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:18.720
They're politicians, they're union workers, they're people who don't get it. They're activists.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.280
And so when you're in journalism you really have to prove yourself before you can join an outlet,

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:28.560
it's very very competitive. There's a lot of people doing it. They're cutting people off from opportunity,

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.040
and what this is going to do is it's just gonna reach these outlets not hiring people from California.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:40.460
This is a really unusual position for people in creative fields like freelance journalism to be in.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:49.400
By nature most of us are liberal, progressive democrats, and we're also pro union for the most part,

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.840
and here we are saying this goes too far.

